    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d659">

                <pb facs="1054" n="934" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg934"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.801/513½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador (Lindsay) to the Assistant
                        Secretary of State (Bundy)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-04-11">April 11, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Bundy</hi>: The Fighting Ship Bill having now
                    been redrafted by its promoters and renumbered H. R. 10674,<anchor n="12"
                        xml:id="d659-f1"/> I am sending you the enclosed Memorandum to put on record
                    that the objections which I had previously urged against H. R. 8874 apply with
                    equal force to the Bill in its new form.<anchor n="13" xml:id="d659-f2"/> It was
                    favourably reported to the House I understand on April 6th.</p>
                <pb facs="1055" n="935" xml:id="pg935"/>
                <p>I also enclose, in case it should be of interest to you, a copy of a letter
                    addressed by the Agent for the Trans-Atlantic Passenger Conference to Mr.
                    Mooney, summing up what transpired at the abortive Conference between the Lines,
                    which sought to reach a compromise.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">R. C. Lindsay</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d659-a1.xml" xpointer="d659-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d659-a2.xml" xpointer="d659-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d659-f1" n="12" xml:id="d659-f1-content">
                <p>Introduced on March 19, by Mr. Ewin L. Davis, Chairman of the Committee on
                    Merchant Marine, Radio, and Fisheries. See <hi rendition="#italic">Congressional
                        Record</hi>, vol. 75, pt. 6, p. 6514.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d659-f2" n="13" xml:id="d659-f2-content">
                <p>Except for Italy, all the countries that lodged formal representations against H.
                    R. 8874 and H. R. 8875 and S. 3501 and S. 3502 (i.e., Great Britain, the
                    Netherlands, Sweden, France, Germany, Canada, and Italy) likewise expressed
                    objections to H. R. 10674.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
